==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|fro|impacience|}} (modern {{m+|fr|impatience}}), from {{der|en|la|impatientia}}. Synchronically analyzable as {{af|en|im-|patience}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɪmˈpeɪʃəns/|lang=en}}
* {{hyph|im|pa|tience|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The quality of being [[impatient]]; lacking [[patience]]; [[restlessness]] and [[intolerance]] of delays; [[anxiety]] and [[eagerness]], especially to begin something.

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|patience}}
* {{l|en|haste}}

